        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "BUCKEYE CHECK CASHING, INC., : Petitioner : v. : No. 04-1264 JOHN CARDEGNA, ET AL."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1264",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bed4e3827b849bec6ae504d98b26cb006dce6a484df45e835a25a5ba7ab4ced8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bed4e3827b84-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:10 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Buckeye Check Cashing, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1264",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bed4e3827b849bec6ae504d98b26cb006dce6a484df45e835a25a5ba7ab4ced8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bed4e3827b84-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case presents the question whether a party can avoid arbitration by challenging the validity of the underlying contract containing an arbitration clause as opposed to the arbitration clause itself."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Buckeye Check Cashing, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1264",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bed4e3827b849bec6ae504d98b26cb006dce6a484df45e835a25a5ba7ab4ced8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bed4e3827b84-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What matters, as a matter of Federal law, is that a challenge to the underlying contract does not allow a court to deny arbitration."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1264",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bed4e3827b849bec6ae504d98b26cb006dce6a484df45e835a25a5ba7ab4ced8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bed4e3827b84-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Does -- does that include a quarrel over offer and acceptance?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1264",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bed4e3827b849bec6ae504d98b26cb006dce6a484df45e835a25a5ba7ab4ced8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bed4e3827b84-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O\u2019CONNOR: Well, Prima Paint did, though, involve what we would characterize as a voidable contract."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Landau (respondent)",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1264",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bed4e3827b849bec6ae504d98b26cb006dce6a484df45e835a25a5ba7ab4ced8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bed4e3827b84-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But clearly, the -- the nub, the crux of their challenge here is a challenge to the legality of the underlying contract. And under their view, they get to obtain judicial resolution of that issue in the first instance, notwithstanding the fact that they don\u2019t dispute that they agreed to arbitrate all issues relating not only to the validity of the arbitration clause itself, but relating to the underlying contract."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1264",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bed4e3827b849bec6ae504d98b26cb006dce6a484df45e835a25a5ba7ab4ced8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bed4e3827b84-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: If the case was one in which the merits issue you claim is basically the same as the legality issue under the contract -- but would your argument be as strong if it were different, if you had a different reason for claiming that the contract was void or voidable?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1264",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bed4e3827b849bec6ae504d98b26cb006dce6a484df45e835a25a5ba7ab4ced8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bed4e3827b84-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: What about the possibility that you always want a neutral decision-maker in cases like this? The arbitrator always has an interest in finding that the contract is valid and arbitrable because that\u2019s his source of business is arbitrating disputes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bland (respondent)",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1264",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bed4e3827b849bec6ae504d98b26cb006dce6a484df45e835a25a5ba7ab4ced8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bed4e3827b84-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court has repeatedly said that Federal law preempts State law only where Congress clearly and manifestly intended for it to do so. And the Court has also repeatedly said that the best guide to what Congress intended was the language of the statutes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1264",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bed4e3827b849bec6ae504d98b26cb006dce6a484df45e835a25a5ba7ab4ced8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bed4e3827b84-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Why?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bland",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1264",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bed4e3827b849bec6ae504d98b26cb006dce6a484df45e835a25a5ba7ab4ced8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bed4e3827b84-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BLAND: Because -- because the language of the statute is what draws the key link difference to me, Your Honor. The statute says an arbitration provision is enforceable if it is in a contract evidencing interstate commerce."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1264",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bed4e3827b849bec6ae504d98b26cb006dce6a484df45e835a25a5ba7ab4ced8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bed4e3827b84-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Mr. Bland, I\u2019m curious to know if you agree with your opponent that whoever decides it, an arbitrator or a judge, it\u2019s really going to be decided by the Florida Supreme Court in the next couple of months."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Landau)",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1264",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bed4e3827b849bec6ae504d98b26cb006dce6a484df45e835a25a5ba7ab4ced8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bed4e3827b84-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LANDAU: Your Honor, I think the word contract is not a precondition in the sense that respondents talk about in the sense that the court has to look into whether it\u2019s a valid contract with all the bells and whistles of State contract law because I think that is entirely inconsistent with Prima Paint."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1264",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bed4e3827b849bec6ae504d98b26cb006dce6a484df45e835a25a5ba7ab4ced8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bed4e3827b84-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: They can logically because they say the arbitration clause, when embedded in a contract that is voidable -- i.e., A and B enter into a contract. B says it\u2019s voidable. I void it. I void it. And there they say, fine, there was a contract and therefore this arbitration clause, which is separable -- you go to arbitration."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1264",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bed4e3827b849bec6ae504d98b26cb006dce6a484df45e835a25a5ba7ab4ced8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bed4e3827b84-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
